---
// The agent guide for people to read; agents get the same text at /agents.md
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ChipIcon from '../assets/chip-icon.svg';
import { Content } from '../lib/agents.md';
const LINK = 'underline decoration-zinc-600 underline-offset-2 hover:text-zinc-100 hover:decoration-zinc-300';
---

<Layout title="Guide for AI agents · Are we ARM yet?" description="How an AI agent helps an ARM laptop's owner check what works under Linux, report it to arewearmyet.com and propose fixes to Omarchy.">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 text-zinc-400 sm:px-6">
    <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-3 text-zinc-300 hover:text-zinc-100">
      <ChipIcon class="h-8 w-8 text-[#9ece6a]" aria-hidden="true" />
      <span class="font-semibold">Are we ARM yet?</span>
    </a>
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-xl bg-[#9ece6a]/10 p-5 text-sm text-zinc-300 ring-1 ring-[#9ece6a]/40">
      Working with an AI agent on your laptop? Tell it: <code class="rounded bg-zinc-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-100">Read https://arewearmyet.com/agents.md and help me check this laptop.</code> The same guide is below, for you to read what it will do. It sends what it finds to arewearmyet.com, without serial numbers, addresses or names, opens pull requests on Omarchy for what it fixes, tries kernel and device tree changes from a boot entry of their own beside your working one, and asks you before changing what you rely on or posting anywhere else.
    </div>
    <article class="guide mt-8">
      <Content />
    </article>
    <p class="mt-10 text-xs text-zinc-500">Plain text for agents: <a class={LINK} href="/agents.md">/agents.md</a> · <a class={LINK} href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a></p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .guide { line-height: 1.7; }
  .guide h1 { color: rgb(250 250 250); font-size: 1.9rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .guide h2 { color: rgb(244 244 245); font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid rgb(39 39 42); scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .guide h3 { color: rgb(228 228 231); font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .guide p, .guide ul, .guide ol, .guide table, .guide pre { margin-top: 0.9rem; }
  .guide ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.4rem; }
  .guide ol { list-style: decimal; padding-left: 1.4rem; }
  .guide li { margin-top: 0.35rem; }
  .guide li::marker { color: rgb(113 113 122); }
  .guide strong { color: rgb(228 228 231); }
  .guide a { text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: rgb(82 82 91); text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .guide a:hover { color: rgb(244 244 245); text-decoration-color: rgb(212 212 216); }
  .guide code { background: rgb(39 39 42); border-radius: 0.25rem; padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem; font-size: 0.85em; color: rgb(228 228 231); }
  .guide pre { background: rgb(9 9 11) !important; border-radius: 0.5rem; padding: 0.9rem; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.55; border: 1px solid rgb(39 39 42); }
  .guide pre code { background: none; padding: 0; font-size: inherit; }
  .guide table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.875rem; display: block; overflow-x: auto; }
  .guide th { text-align: left; color: rgb(228 228 231); font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(63 63 70); padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem 0.5rem 0; }
  .guide td { border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(39 39 42); padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem 0.5rem 0; vertical-align: top; }
</style>
